{#
  The dog-gear block (docs/DECISIONS.md 0013, narrowed by 0014). Included by
  dogs.html.jinja only; no lake, county, state or other page includes it.
  Renders nothing while AMAZON_ASSOCIATE_TAG in site.py is empty (gear_links is
  then an empty list). As on Trout Truck, the "Affiliate links" label and the
  disclosure come before the links. Plain Amazon search links, never a product,
  never a price, and never a home toxin test kit.
#}
{% if gear_links %}
<section class="gear" aria-labelledby="gear-heading">
  <p class="muted">Affiliate links</p>
  <h2 id="gear-heading">Gear that helps you follow this advice</h2>
  <p>
    These links search Amazon for dog gear that goes with the advice above.
    They point to search results, not to any one product. No gear changes
    what is in the water or protects your dog from it: keep your dog out of
    water that has an advisory on file, or that looks green, blue-green or
    scummy.
  </p>
  <p class="muted" id="gear-disclosure">
    These are affiliate links: if you buy something after following one, this
    site earns a commission, and it costs you nothing extra.
    {{ amazon_disclosure }}
    {{ gear_endorsement }}
    <a href="{{ root }}privacy/#affiliate">More in the privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    {% for g in gear_links %}
    <li><a href="{{ g.url }}" rel="{{ affiliate_rel }}">{{ g.label }}</a>: {{ g.why }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{% endif %}
